    "rationale": "The undiluted readings are flat at about 0.42 from 6 to 18 h, with a sharp stop after rapid growth. That pattern is consistent with a reader that stops responding at high density. I had budget for one read only: the 18 h aliquot at 10x dilution gave 0.0472, which scales to about 0.47. That is about 12% above the undiluted reading of about 0.42 (0.4199 at 18 h; the 6–18 h mean is about 0.42). The undiluted readings scatter by only about 2%, so the gap is probably larger than noise, but with a single replicate I can't be sure. The size of the excess suggests only mild compression. Overall I lean towards biomass being above the reading, with moderate confidence."
